WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.890
The Aurora Borealis, otherwise known as The
Northern Lights are one of nature’s most

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:12.420
beautiful displays of omnipotence. Despite
what its name suggests, The Northern Lights

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:18.330
can be seen almost anywhere in the world,
even as far south as the equator. The phenomenon

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:23.980
has been witnessed in Honolulu and Singapore.
However, sightings that far south are extremely

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.070
rare, it’s most commonly witnessed within
the Arctic Circle. The South Pole also has

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:35.100
its own version of the Aurora Borealis, called
the Aurora Australis. And Earth isn’t the

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.480
only planet with aurora, you would witness
a similar phenomenon if you were to stand

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:47.309
on Jupiter or Saturn. Uranus has aurora too,
but unlike the other planets with their wave-like

00:00:47.309 --> 00:00:53.230
aurora, the aurora on Uranus would look like
glowing dots… and yes, I am talking about

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:59.390
the planet. But what exactly causes these
mysterious light shows? Let’s find out.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:09.080
Some Inuit believe that the spirits of their
ancestors can be seen dancing within the lights

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:14.909
of the Aurora. The Vikings believed that the
Aurora was a bridge of fire to the sky, forged

00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:20.820
by the gods. Well, spoiler alert, according
to modern science, the northern and southern

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:25.900
lights are not dancing spirits or a bridge
of fire. They are actually caused by something

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.590
much more tangible, the Sun.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:37.270
Our Sun is a 4.57 billion-year-old ball of
hydrogen and other gasses fusing away in space,

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:43.880
150 million kilometres away from planet Earth.
And every once in a while it kicks up a bit

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:50.540
of a storm, a Solar Storm to be precise. The
Sun produces energy by smashing hydrogen atoms

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:55.630
together in its core, under such immense temperatures
and pressures, to cause the hydrogen atoms

00:01:55.630 --> 00:02:03.680
to fuse, to form helium atoms. This process
is known as nuclear fusion. When atoms are

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.750
under these kinds of pressures they turn into
a mushy soup of freely moving particles, which

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:15.500
is a fourth state of matter known as plasma.
The Sun is essentially a gigantic ball of

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.550
swirling plasma.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:22.260
Using the process of nuclear fusion, the Sun
is able to turn small amounts of matter into

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:27.230
enormous quantities of energy. It’s how
the Sun has managed to keep producing energy

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:33.500
for billions of years without running out
of fuel. If human-kind were able to consistently

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:38.610
replicate nuclear-fusion here on Earth, we
would be able to make almost infinite amounts

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:44.750
of energy, using relatively little resources.
In fact, if you could convert the mass of

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:53.830
one bag of sugar into energy it would be enough
to drive a car, non-stop, for 100,000 years.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:58.890
All this plasma swirling around within the
Sun generates huge magnetic fields. These

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:04.290
magnetic fields are under such immense pressures
within the Sun, that sometimes the lines of

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:10.790
force of theses magnetic fields meet. When
this happens, the magnetic field is forced

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:16.700
outwards, towards the surface of the Sun.
Once it reaches the Sun’s surface it ejects

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:22.530
outwards into space at great speeds, taking
extremely hot gasses and charged particles,

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:28.760
also known as plasma, with it. This is known
as a solar flare and they can be witnessed

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:35.379
on the Sun’s surface as a very bright spot
followed by a cloud of gas. When a very large

00:03:35.379 --> 00:03:41.440
solar flare occurs containing a significantly
huge amount of energy, it is referred to as

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:49.629
a Coronal Mass Ejection or CME for short.
The gas clouds produced by a CME can sometimes

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.480
be larger than the Sun itself.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:58.569
CME’s and solar flares don’t stop just
outside the Sun’s surface. Charged particles

00:03:58.569 --> 00:04:04.030
ejected from the Sun continue to travel outwards
through space over enormous distances. After

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:09.080
travelling through space for around two days
they will reach planet Earth. This is known

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:17.299
as the solar wind and it can be extremely
dangerous. If the magnetic field released

00:04:17.299 --> 00:04:23.680
from a solar flare or CME were to hit planet
Earth it could cause the extinction of the

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:30.370
human race. So why hasn’t it? After all
solar flares are taking place regularly on

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.820
the Sun’s surface.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:40.360
Well the solar wind does actually hit Earth,
often, but our trusty planet is well-prepared.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:45.889
We have a defence system to protect us from
the huge amounts of energy the Sun bombards

00:04:45.889 --> 00:04:51.639
us with on a daily basis. Just like the Sun,
the Earth produces its own magnetic field.

00:04:51.639 --> 00:05:00.479
At the Earth’s core is a ball of solid iron,
the heat of this iron turns the surrounding

00:05:00.479 --> 00:05:07.199
outer core into flowing liquid iron. The movement
of this outer liquid core produces a magnetic

00:05:07.199 --> 00:05:11.479
field, that, luckily for us, encompasses the
Earth.

00:05:11.479 --> 00:05:16.259
The Earth’s magnetic field protects us from
all sorts of harsh destructive forces that

00:05:16.259 --> 00:05:21.889
come from far away in space, including solar
flares. This protective barrier is called

00:05:21.889 --> 00:05:27.910
the Earth’s magnetosphere and it extends
thousands of kilometres into space. That sounds

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:34.259
large, but it’s actually rather modest,
Jupiter’s magnetosphere extends over seven

00:05:34.259 --> 00:05:41.060
million kilometres into space on each side
of the planet. In fact, on Jupiter’s nightside,

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:47.350
the side facing away from the Sun, the magnetic
field which is emitted is so large, that it

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:48.960
reaches Saturn.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.860
Anyway, back to Earth. Most of the Sun’s
solar winds simply bounce off the Earth’s

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:59.949
magnetosphere when it reaches us. However,
the magnetosphere has two weak spots, at the

00:05:59.949 --> 00:06:06.389
north and south poles. At these two locations
the magnetic fields which protect planet Earth

00:06:06.389 --> 00:06:10.660
are much less prevalent than nearer the equator.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:15.620
This means that a very small percentage of
the charged particles that come from the Sun

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:21.229
do make their way into the Earth’s atmosphere
via the two weak spots at the poles. When

00:06:21.229 --> 00:06:27.000
this happens the electrons in the solar wind
collide with oxygen and nitrogen atoms in

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:32.180
the Earth’s atmosphere. During this interaction
energy is transferred from the atoms in the

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:38.650
solar wind to the Earth’s oxygen and nitrogen
atoms. Raising these atom’s energy states

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:44.550
and exciting them. When an atom gets excited
its electrons move into an orbit further away

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.400
from the nucleus.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:51.370
These newly excited atoms need to release
this new found energy to “calm themselves

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:57.750
down” and return to their baseline energy
state. The oxygen and nitrogen atoms release

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:02.810
this energy in the form of particles of light
or photons. The light they give out is what

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:08.759
we call the aurora. This process of exciting
atoms to cause them to release energy in the

00:07:08.759 --> 00:07:15.300
form of light is the exact same way that neon
lights work. The aurora are simply mother

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:21.069
nature’s neon lights, executed on a far
grander scale. The only difference is that

00:07:21.069 --> 00:07:26.389
nature uses this phenomenon in a far subtler
way than to advertise strip bars.

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:32.680
The aurora typically appears in vast curtains
or waves of light following a distinct line

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:38.580
across the sky. They appear this way because
they are following lines of force in the Earth’s

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:44.879
magnetic field. Yep, that’s right, the aurora
uses the force.

00:07:44.879 --> 00:07:49.830
The different colours of the aurora are caused
by different gases in the atmosphere. Each

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:55.720
gas emits a unique colour when it is excited.
For example, oxygen gives off a green light

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:01.050
when it’s excited, which is the most common
colour seen in the aurora. Nitrogen on the

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:05.030
other hand, gives of blue and red colours
when excited.

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:11.210
So to summarise, when charged particles released
from the solar flares on the Sun’s surface

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:16.870
hit our planet at either the north or south
pole, they interact with atoms in the Earth’s

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:22.560
atmostphere. Causing their electrons to move
to a higher energy state. When the electrons

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:28.160
drop back down to a lower energy state they
release photons, tiny little particles of

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:33.959
light, which light up the night’s sky in
a spectacular display of painted waves, following

00:08:33.959 --> 00:08:38.060
the natural magnetic field lines of planet
Earth.

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:43.789
Knowing how the aurora are formed may spoil
the beauty for you, but I believe there’s

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:48.800
an even greater beauty in understanding the
science behind one of nature’s most breathtaking

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:55.510
performances. So if you’re ever lucky enough
to experience the aurora for yourself, just

00:08:55.510 --> 00:09:01.690
take a moment to contemplate on how truly
marvellous and magnificent the universe really

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.700
is …and then take selfies.

